  "electrical": {
   "title": "MELTED WIRING",
   "sub": "POWER FOR THE HYDRAULICS",
   "track": "Hollywood waves",
   "text": "The pump looks fine, but the deck still won't move? Sometimes the problem isn't hydraulic at all. It's electrical. At Car Hauler Repair Houston we track down melted wiring at the pump, bad grounds and failing solenoids, the small parts that decide whether your hydraulics get power. We handle trailer wiring from a single connector to a complete rewire, including marker lights, rear lights, light boxes, switches and batteries. So why troubleshoot the whole circuit instead of splicing one wire? Because the goal is power you can trust, not a patch that quits on the next load. We find what's damaged, fix it, and hand the rig back with the hydraulics powered safely and the lights working. Electrical gremlins? Text or call the shop.",
