  "leakdown": {
   "title": "LEAKS DOWN OVERNIGHT",
   "sub": "CYLINDERS, VALVES & PTO",
   "track": "Kama Sutra",
   "text": "You park it loaded at night, and by morning the deck has crept down. That's not bad luck. That's a leak. At Car Hauler Repair Houston we chase down the cause: scored or bent cylinders, tired valves, weeping fittings and damaged lines. A cylinder that can be saved is rebuilt with new seals and components, and one that can't is replaced. And if the PTO engages but nothing moves? That's a pressure problem, and we trace it back through the pump until full pressure reaches the deck again. Hoses are crimped in-house, so most of these repairs don't wait on a supplier. The goal is simple: set it loaded, and it holds all night. Deck drifting on you? Call before the next load.",
